==History==
2016
*The Freeze [[Cards|card]] was added with Clash Royale's game launch on 4/1/2016.
*On 2/2/2016, the [[Version History#February 2016 Update (2/2/2016)|February 2016 Update]] decreased the Freeze's area radius to 3 tiles (from 4 tiles) and the duration would increase 0.3 seconds per level (from 0.4 seconds).
*On 3/5/2016, the [[Version History#May%202016%20Update%20(3/5/2016)|May 2016 Update]], changed the visual effects of the Freeze.
*On 18/5/2016, a [[Version History#Balance%20Changes%20(18/5/2016)|Balance Update]], decreased the Freeze's duration by 1 second.
*On 4/7/2016, the [[Version History#Tournaments Update (4/7/2016)|Tournaments Update]], allowed the Freeze to stop the [[Elixir Collector]]'s [[Elixir]] generation and reset the [[Inferno Tower]]'s damage output.
2018
*On 25/4/2018, the [[Version History#Clan%20Wars%20Update%20(25/4/2018)|Clan Wars Update]], allowed the Freeze to be placed on the river.
*On 20/6/2018, the [[Version History#Summer%202018%20Update%20(20/6/2018)|Summer 2018 Update]], moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Freeze from P.E.K.K.A's Playhouse to Spell Valley.
*On 3/9/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (3/9/2018)|Balance Update]], made it so that the Freeze can no longer reset the attack of the [[Zappies]].
*On 5/9/2018, the [[Version History#September%202018%20Update%20(5/9/2018)|September 2018 Update]], changed it so that {{Rarity|Epic}} cards start at Level 6 and end at Level 13 (from 1 to 8).
*On 5/12/2018, the [[Version History#December%202018%20Update%20(5/12/2018)|December 2018 Update]], set the Freeze's duration to 5 seconds for every Level and made the [[:Category:Spell Cards|spell]] deal area damage. Its description was also changed slightly. Previously, its description was "''Freezes troops and buildings, making them unable to move or attack. Everybody chill.''".
2019
*On 7/1/2019, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (7/1/2019)|Balance Update]], made it so that the Freeze would only deal 35% of its full damage to [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Towers]].
*On 28/1/2019, the [[Version History#January 2019 Update (28/1/2019)|January 2019 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Freeze from Spell Valley to Frozen Peak.
*On 4/2/2019, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (4/2/2019)|Balance Update]], decreased the Freeze's duration to 4 seconds (from 5 seconds) and decreased its damage by 6%.
*On 26/11/2019, the [[Version History#End%20of%20November%202019%20Update%20(26/11/2019)|End of November 2019 Update]], removed the Freeze from [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Mega Deck]] [[Touchdown]].
2020
*On 4/8/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (4/8/2020)|Balance Update]], decreased the Freeze's Crown Tower damage to 30% of the full damage (from 35%).
2021
*On 7/6/2021, the [[Version History#Summer%202021%20Update%20(7/6/2021)|Summer 2021 Update]], slightly changed the Freeze's description, adding the phrase “''Reduced damage to Crown Towers.''” to it.
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
2023
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
*On 13/11/2023, a [[Version History#Minor%20Update%20(13/11/2023)|Minor Update]], made it so that frozen [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] can no longer be pushed by others.
2025
*On 24/11/2025, the 2025 Quarter 4 Update added a card render to the Freeze's card info screen.
*On 1/12/2025, a Balance Update increased Freeze's damage by 29%.
2026

* On 1/6/2026, a Balance Update, decreased the Freeze's Crown Tower damage to 25% of the full damage (from 30%)

==Trivia==
*The Freeze resembles the real life chemical [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nitrogen Nitrogen (N)], a gas that, at a temperature of 63 Kelvin, significantly below freezing levels, is a colorless liquid that is used as a coolant, just like the Freeze.
*The Freeze is 1 of 7 [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]] which first existed in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Earthquake]], [[Heal]], [[Lightning]], [[Poison]], [[Rage]], and [[Clone]].
**Barring its damage, the Freeze has the exact same characteristics as its [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Freeze_Spell Clash of Clans counterpart].
**The bottle of it resembles its older version of the Freeze spell that took 2 housing spaces.
*The Freeze is 1 of 7 [[cards]] associated with ice, with the others being [[Ice Spirit]], [[Giant Snowball]], [[Ice Golem]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Super Ice Golem]], and [[Wizard Trio]].
**In the German and Spanish language settings of the game, the Freeze's name translates to "Frost". In the Italian, Norwegian, Turkish, and Finnish language settings of the game, the Freeze's name translates to "Freezing". In the Persian and Indonesian language settings of the game, the Freeze's name translates to "Freezer". In the Korean and Portuguese language settings of the game, the Freeze's name translates to "Ice Magic" and"Ice" respectively.
**A Trainer in the [[Training Camp]] is called Trainer Freeze and uses 4 ice-related cards in their [[Battle Decks|deck]], one of them being Freeze, and the others being Ice Spirit, Giant Snowball, and Ice Golem.
*[[:Category:Troop Cards|Troops]] frozen by the Freeze will remain frozen even if they are pushed out of the Freeze's radius.
*When the Freeze spell has been cast, a pale circle marking its radius will appear with some snow on the border. The circle line outside the radius will be team-colored.
**The Freeze is 1 of 7 spells which have team-colored rings on their radius, the others are Earthquake, Poison, Rage, Clone, [[Tornado]], and [[Graveyard]].
*According to Darian Vorlick, the Community Manager of Clash of Clans, the Freeze is his favorite spell, as stated in [https://youtu.be/tt3I0PaqZCo?t=174 Clash of Clans Throughout the Years] video.
*If the [[Tesla]] is about to retreat and the Freeze is used on it, the retreating sound effect will [https://www.youtube.com/shorts/7okIFPURFRA loop].
*The Freeze has been featured in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]] outside of the card. More specifically:
**The Freeze is 1 of 4 spells that have been featured in the [[Global Spell]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being Heal, Lightning, and Rage.
***In the Snowstorm sub-mode of the Global Spell game mode, the Global Freeze lasts permanently instead of 4 seconds.
**The Freeze is 1 of 5 spells that have been featured in the [[Treasure Hunt#Spell%20Cauldron|Spell Cauldron]] sub-mode of the [[Treasure Hunt]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being Heal, Lightning, Rage, and Clone.
*The Freeze is featured in non-Clash games. More specifically:
**The Freeze is featured as a spell in [https://www.chess.com/ Chess], in a chess variant called [https://www.chess.com/variants Spell Chess.]
**Although not available as a spell, the Freeze reappears as [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Ice_Wizard Ice Wizard]'s active ability in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*It is 1 of 20 cards that is unavailable in [[Mirror]] mode, the others being [[Minions]], [[Cannon]], [[Mortar]], Tesla, [[Goblin Hut]], [[Tombstone]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Inferno Tower]], [[Barbarian Hut]], [[Furnace]], [[Elixir Collector]], Clone, [[X-Bow]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Mighty Miner]], [[Little Prince]], and the [[Monk]].
*The Freeze is the subject of a few [[Clans|Clan]] badges.
*The Freeze was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/pRfrjMiHbQA?si=P2kVLJUlXH1SZoHm Clash Royale League 2021 Tournament], by a player called Mugi.
*Before the Freeze's card release, the Freeze's duration was decreased by 1 second.

